    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d225">

                <pb facs="0332" n="234" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg234"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">033.1132/55: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morgan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-12-23T10:00:00-03:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 23,
                                1920—10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 1:55
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>128. Please say to the President that the results of Secretary Colby’s visit to
                    Brazil promise to be all that he could desire.<anchor n="89" xml:id="d225-f1"/>
                    His felicitous and discreet addresses yesterday to the Senate, to the House and
                    to the American Chamber of Commerce as well as his toast at the dinner which the
                    President offered him in Barbadotete [<hi rendition="#italic">Cattete?</hi>]
                    Palace on the night of his arrival were characterized by devotion to the ideals,
                    principles and person of the President. The Secretary is meeting the best men of
                    the country under happy conditions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morgan</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d225-f1" n="89" xml:id="d225-f1-content">
                <p>The Secretary was in Brazil Dec. 21–25.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
